<section>
  <h2>Common Questions About PDF Compression</h2>

  <h3>Does compression affect quality?</h3>
  <p>With our "Balanced" or "High Quality" settings, you won't notice any difference in quality. Text remains sharp, images stay clear, and formatting is preserved. The "Maximum" setting may show slight artifacts on complex images, but it's usually unnoticeable for most documents.</p>

  <h3>Is my data safe?</h3>
  <p>Absolutely. Our tool processes everything in your browser using JavaScript. Your files never leave your device - we don't even see them. This makes our compressor perfect for sensitive business documents.</p>

  <h3>Why can't I compress more?</h3>
  <p>Some PDFs are already "compressed" (using internal compression algorithms). There's a physical limit to how much you can reduce a file. In these cases, you might need to remove pages or convert images to smaller formats.</p>
</section>

